                "quoted_status_profile_username": null,
                "reply_count": 1,
                "retweet_count": 0,
                "source": "Twitter for iPhone",
                "text": "60 years ago today, Medicare and Medicaid became law, transforming health care in America. Since then, these programs have provided generations of Americans with access to the care they need and the dignity they deserve. Today, over 140 million people rely on them. Nearly half of all births nationwide are covered by Medicaid, and Medicare supports more than 60 million seniors and people with disabilities.\n\nBut that progress is under threat. Donald Trump and Republicans in Congress are pushing an extreme agenda that would rip health care away from over 15 million Americans, slash protections, and drive up costs\u2014just to give more tax breaks to the wealthy.\n\nFor 60 years, Medicare and Medicaid have been lifelines for seniors, people with disabilities, children, new mothers, and low-income families. I will never stop fighting to protect and strengthen these programs, because health care is a right, not a privilege.",
                "text_lang": "en",
                "text_tagged_users": null,
                "text_tagged_users_ids": null,
                "text_tags": null,
